---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What languages and frameworks does MC support?",
    answer: "Any codebase that AI coding agents can work with. MC orchestrates the agents — it doesn't care if your project is TypeScript, Python, Go, or Rust. If Claude Code or another agent can build in it, MC can govern it.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which AI models are supported?",
    answer: "Currently optimized for Anthropic's Claude family (Opus, Sonnet, Haiku) with risk-tier routing — the right model for the right task. Support for additional model providers is on the roadmap.",
  },
  {
    question: "How do I define policies?",
    answer: "Policies are YAML configuration files in your repo. You define quality gates (lint, test coverage, security scans), risk tiers (which changes need which model), and escalation rules. MC ships with sensible defaults — most teams customize from there.",
  },
  {
    question: "What does the pilot engagement look like?",
    answer: "4 weeks. We deploy MC on one of your repos, configure policies together, and run the first 50 PRs. You measure the delta — velocity, quality, cost. If the numbers don't work, you walk away. No lock-in.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is my code sent to external services?",
    answer: "Your code goes to the AI model provider (Anthropic) for processing — same as if your developers used Claude directly. MC itself runs on your infrastructure (self-hosted) or on a dedicated instance we manage. We never store your source code.",
  },
  {
    question: "How is MC different from just using Claude Code directly?",
    answer: "Claude Code is a single agent, single task. MC is the fleet manager — it handles parallel execution, policy enforcement, risk-tier routing, evidence collection, and Temporal-based reliability across hundreds of tasks. Think of it as the difference between one developer and an engineering org.",
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-center mb-4">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-center mb-12">
      Don't see your question? <a href="mailto:sergey@kovalev.dev" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">Email me directly</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] hover:border-[var(--border-hover)] transition-colors">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-6 text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium select-none">
            <span>{faq.question}</span>
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[var(--text-muted)] shrink-0 ml-4 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm leading-relaxed -mt-2">
            {faq.answer}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
